# Plane Project Structure Guide

Plane is an open-source project management tool built with a modern monorepo architecture. This guide helps navigate the codebase structure.

## Architecture Overview

Plane uses a **monorepo architecture** with multiple applications and shared packages:

### Applications (`apps/`)
- **`web/`** - Main Next.js frontend application (port 3000)
- **`space/`** - Documentation/knowledge base app (port 3002) 
- **`admin/`** - Admin interface (port 3001)
- **`api/`** - Django REST API backend
- **`live/`** - Real-time collaboration server (Node.js)
- **`proxy/`** - Caddy reverse proxy configuration

### Shared Packages (`packages/`)
- **`@plane/ui`** - Shared UI components library
- **`@plane/types`** - TypeScript type definitions
- **`@plane/services`** - API service layer
- **`@plane/constants`** - Application constants
- **`@plane/hooks`** - Custom React hooks
- **`@plane/utils`** - Utility functions
- **`@plane/editor`** - Rich text editor components
- **`@plane/i18n`** - Internationalization
- **`@plane/propel`** - Design system components

## Key Files
- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Root package configuration with workspaces
- [turbo.json](mdc:turbo.json) - Turborepo build configuration
- [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml) - Development environment setup
- [apps/web/next.config.js](mdc:apps/web/next.config.js) - Next.js configuration

## Development Workflow
- Use `yarn dev` to start all applications
- Each app has its own package.json with specific dependencies
- Shared packages are built and linked automatically
- Turbo handles build orchestration and caching

## Technology Stack
- **Frontend**: Next.js 14, React 18, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- **Backend**: Django REST Framework, Python
- **State Management**: MobX
- **Build System**: Turborepo, tsup
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS, Headless UI
- **Real-time**: WebSockets (Node.js server)